-- Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two, five hovercycles (printed 167-176): Rampage, Streetrunner, Windfire, Wave Cutter, Windshark
-- 5 vehicle rows, with 53 locations and 9 weapon entries.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~317-northern-gun-2-hovercycles-b.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/vessel-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every value
-- is printable ASCII, every row cites its book, and a Main Body location
-- agrees with its vehicle's mdc_main_body.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
  ('ng-320-rampage-hovercycle', 'NG-320 Rampage Winged Combat Hovercycle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One rider.', 'None; no space for a passenger.', NULL, 'Maximum 180 mph (288 km). Maximum altitude 90 ft (27.4 m), though it usually hovers 3-12 ft (0.9 to 3.7 m) up; handles drops of up to 1,500 ft (457 m). -5% piloting per 30 ft (9.1 m) above the ground. A hover vehicle; the book prints one speed.', NULL, 'Height 5.9 ft (1.8 m); length 8.5 ft (2.6 m); width 10.6 ft (3.23 m) across the wings (the prose rounds it to ten and a half feet, 3.2 m)', '1,126 lbs (507 kg)', 155, 1, NULL, 379000, '379,000 credits gasoline, 455,000 electric, 845,000 Solid Oxide, 1.4 million nuclear with a 10 year life; the lowest is stored. The dual nose gun and both wing guns are standard; a bike without them is a custom order 100,000 credits cheaper with a 2D6+10 day wait. Added weapons cost extra and are never discounted.', 'Model NG-320, new (Vehicle Type: Winged Combat Hovercycle). A conventional-looking hovercycle given stubby wings and extra thrusters for control in racing and stunts, and armoured heavily enough for adventuring; a hit with mercenaries, explorers, Juicers, Headhunters, raiders, bandits, pirates and other men-at-arms, less so with City Rats and street crooks, though it would make a good police interceptor. Its design team was led by Andy "Fly Boy" McElvary, with Michael Barakofsky and Daniel Garza; it stops short, takes punishment in the field and makes dead drops from 1,500 ft (457 m). Dodge: +1 under 100 mph (160 km), +2 faster. Penalties: -5% piloting for sudden stops, tricks, stunts or evasion; none for the built-in weapons, the usual for add-ons. The wings make it about 10.5 ft wide, so narrow alleys are closed to it and in forest it must ride above the treetops; it is at its best on prairie and desert and in the open New West, Southwest and northern Mexico. Each wing thruster lost costs 15% of top speed and altitude, -3% piloting (doubled when both on one side are gone) and 15% of the dead drop; the entry also says one lost with its wing intact costs 10% of speed and -5% piloting. With all four thrusters gone it still hovers, at 72 mph (115 km) and no higher than 48 ft (14.6 m). Losing one wing: -10% speed, -12% piloting; both: -30% speed, -24% piloting (the location list prints four wings). Optional weapons: one more on each front side, 5% of speed each, and not recommended. Long-range communications: the right-side antenna links helmet radios and extends any short-range set to 50 miles (80 km). Range: 1,000 miles (1,600 km). Power: usually combustion or electric, nuclear available; a Solid Oxide version is priced. Never bought by the CS military; very popular with men-at-arms and buyers in open country.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.167-168'),
  ('ng-150-streetrunner-hovercycle', 'NG-150 Streetrunner Hovercycle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One rider.', 'None.', NULL, 'Maximum 150 mph (240 km). Maximum altitude 20 ft (6.1 m); handles drops from as high as 220 ft (67 m). A hover vehicle; the book prints one speed.', NULL, 'Height 2.8 ft (0.85 m); width 2.6 ft (0.79 m); length 6 ft 9 in (2 m), a foot (0.3 m) of it the nose bar', '110 lbs (49.5 kg); twice that with deluxe armor', 60, 1, NULL, 61000, '61,000 credits gasoline, 91,000 electric, 153,000 solar with backup electric batteries; no Solid Oxide or nuclear version. Deluxe armored model: 30% more. Weapons cost extra and are never discounted.', 'Model NG-150 (Vehicle Type: Hovercycle). A light, quick and cheap one-person bike made for the city: sudden stops, tight turns, back alleys, sewer tunnels and the ruins of fallen buildings. City Rats, Operators, Cyber-Snatchers out of the ''Burbs, Quick Flex Aliens, couriers, drug runners, crooks and teenagers took to it at once. Handling: +10% piloting, +1 on initiative, +2 to dodge, and its penalties for evasion and trick riding are halved. Penalties: -5% piloting for sudden stops, tricks, stunts or evasion; each mounted weapon costs -5% piloting and as much speed, a multi-shot missile pod -10%, and anything past three weapons another -10%. No weapons as standard: one may be added in the nose and one on each side, each costing 5% of speed. Deluxe armored model: 30% more main body M.D.C. (printed as 90), 30% more cost, 10% less speed and double the weight. Range: 600 miles (960 km). Power: a combustion or electric engine, or solar with backup batteries. Never bought or used by the CS.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.170-171'),
  ('ng-500-windfire-hovercycle', 'NG-500 Windfire Heavy Combat Hovercycle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One rider.', 'One, cramped (-5% piloting).', 'Land speed 130 mph; the book prints (256 km), which does not convert (130 mph is about 208 km). Maximum altitude 60 ft (18.3 m), though it usually hovers 3-12 ft (0.9 to 3.6 m) up; handles drops of up to 500 ft (152 m). -5% piloting per 30 ft (9.1 m) above the ground.', NULL, NULL, 'Height 5.4 ft (1.65 m); wingspan 9.4 ft (2.87 m), though the prose calls it 11 ft (3.3 m) wide; length 14 ft overall (printed 4.6 m)', '1,456 lbs (655 kg)', 165, 1, NULL, 1900000, '1.9 million credits, nuclear only with a 10 year life, the exclusive weapons included. Nothing can be added.', 'Model NG-500, new (Vehicle Type: Winged Heavy Combat Hovercycle). A costly experiment from a team led by Andy McElvary with Peter Michalaenka and Thomas Andary: nuclear power only and heavy built-in firepower, a low quad laser array and a big nose cannon set among four mini-missile tubes, with no room or need for anything more. The load makes it nose heavy and slower than most hovercycles, though it stays quick and hits hard; four stubby wings help at racing speed and in stunts, and heavy armour fits it for very hostile country. Its price has kept sales slow while its reputation grows; the CS has asked that it stay a rare, low-production item and bans it, as do most civilized places, so it is not street legal. Favoured by combat cyborgs, RPA pilots, Headhunters, mercenaries, gunfighters, lawmen, raiders, bandits, pirates and big or combat-minded D-Bees. Dodge: +1 under 100 mph (160 km), +2 faster. Penalties: -5% piloting for sudden stops, tricks, stunts or evasion. At about 11 ft wide it cannot use narrow alleys and in forest must clear the treetops; it does best on prairie, desert and open land. Each lower wing thruster lost costs 15% of top speed and altitude, -3% piloting and 15% of the dead drop. Losing one of the big side thrusters costs 30% of speed; losing both and the wing thrusters leaves it crawling on its undercarriage jets at -30% piloting with no tricks or evasion, and with every thruster gone it hovers at 15 mph (24 km), no higher than 4 ft (1.2 m). Each wing lost with its thruster intact: -2% speed, -5% piloting. Armour is heaviest at the nose. Range: unlimited. Never bought or used by the CS.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.172-173'),
  ('ng-su600-wave-cutter-hovercycle', 'NG-SU600-EX Wave Cutter Submersible Hovercycle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One pilot.', 'One.', 'Maximum 100 mph (160 km) on land; handles drops of up to 300 ft (91.5 m). Hovers up to 20 ft (6.1 m) above ground or waves; cannot fly.', NULL, 'Surface 70 mph (112 km); underwater 40 mph (64 km or 34.7 knots). Depth tolerance 1,000 ft (305 m) plus 1D4x100 ft (30.5 to 122 m); deeper, the hull splits and floods and the pilot risks the bends (save vs death on 15 or better).', 'Height 5 ft (1.5 m); width 3 ft (0.9 m); length 9 ft (2.7 m)', '1,400 lbs (630 kg)', 140, 1, NULL, 585000, '585,000 credits electric battery or gasoline, 680,000 Solid Oxide, 1.6 million nuclear; the lowest is stored. No weapons can be added.', 'Model NG-SU600-EX, new (Class: Hover-Capable Light Submersible; the heading prints NG-SU600). A small, fast one-pilot craft drawn from the NG Aquapod, joining its submarine hull to a hover-lift system so it runs along beaches and over land, skims water like a boat, then cuts the hover and dives. Designed by Frederick Meyer, Nathan Bingham and Benjamin Rodriguez; navies, sailors, pirates and privateers want it, raiders most of all, since it can hit ships from below without warning and wreck props or rudders, and aircraft cannot follow it under. Fully enclosed, it shields the pilot from cold, water and pressure, but its depth and air are limited and it needs care below the surface. Dodge: +1 under 100 mph (160 km), +2 faster. Penalties: -5% for sudden stops, fast dives, tricks, stunts or evasion. Sensors and features: the environmental systems of power armor without radar or targeting; a depth and pressure gauge alarmed at 900 ft (274 m); nine hours of recycled, heated air; a 5 mile (8 km) radio; a 96-hour distress beacon; a nose searchlight pivoting 30 degrees (600 ft/183 m underwater); identification lights, two at the rear and two underneath; a rear tow line for riding behind ships or hauling finds off the bottom; sonar tracking 64 targets out to 50 miles (80 km). Cargo: space for a couple of backpacks, a survival kit and a rifle. Power: nuclear (about 10 years), Solid Oxide or electric battery.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.173-175'),
  ('ng-640-windshark-hovercycle', 'NG-640 Windshark Amphibious Hovercycle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One pilot.', 'One; uncomfortable on long trips.', 'Land speed 150 mph (240 km). Maximum altitude 60 ft (18.3 m), though it usually hovers 3-12 ft (0.9 to 3.6 m) up; handles drops of up to 500 ft (152 m). -5% piloting per 30 ft (9.1 m) above the ground.', NULL, '80 mph (128 km) riding over the surface on its air cushion. No underwater capability: submerged, it sinks.', 'Height 4 ft (1.2 m); width 4 ft (1.2 m) with the pontoons deployed; length 6.7 ft (2 m)', '635 lbs (285.7 kg)', 122, 1, NULL, 269000, '269,000 credits gasoline, 345,000 electric, 1.3 million nuclear with a 10 year life; the lowest is stored. Every price includes the standard weapons.', 'Model NG-640 (Class: Amphibious Hovercycle). A small, very fast amphibious hovercycle from Demetrius Karanikolos, Brandon Pack and Matthew Clements, one of several NG amphibious vehicles; popular at once with dockworkers, naval crews, sailors, pirates and privateers on the coasts, the Mississippi and the Great Lakes, and with Wilderness Scouts, explorers, trappers and adventurers in lake and marsh country such as Dinosaur Swamp. Not a submersible: it crosses water of any depth on an air cushion. To stop on water it hovers in place or settles on two large pontoon landing skis, which fold in against the body when not needed. Two booster jets give lift when the hover drive cuts out over water; their housings seal if it is briefly swamped and drive against the water to lift it clear without losing power. Stronger undercarriage jets carry it over and through rough seas. Switched off over water with the pontoons up, or driven under, it sinks. Dodge: +1 under 100 mph (160 km), +2 faster. Penalties: -5% piloting for sudden stops, tricks, stunts or evasion. Features: 5 mile (8 km) radio and a 96-hour distress beacon; two waterproof saddlebags, each holding a rifle, a survival kit or the like. Optional weapons: only a second pair of mini-missile/torpedo tubes on the nose sides, four tubes at most. Range: 860 miles (1,376 km) on fuel or battery, unlimited on nuclear. Engine: usually combustion or electric, nuclear available. Never bought or used by the CS. The hovercycle list on p.161 prints the model as NG-SU640-EX; the Contents and the entry''s Model Type line print NG-640, followed here.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.175-176');

